      "properties": {
        "reported": true,
        "property_type": "magnetic",
        "summary": "Dc susceptibility of 2 under 1000 Oe (2–300 K): χmT = 113.44 cm3·K·mol−1 at room temperature (calc. 118.1 for 15 uncoupled Gd(III), S=7/2, g=2), remaining nearly constant to ~60 K then falling to 73.2 cm3·K·mol−1 at 2 K, indicating antiferromagnetic Gd···Gd interactions. Curie–Weiss fit (50–300 K): C = 114.91 cm3·K·mol−1, θ = −1.27 K. Magnetization reaches 86.6 NμB at 2 K and 7 T without saturation (expected 105 NμB). Magnetocaloric −ΔSm max = 29.9 J·kg−1·K−1 at 3 K and 7 T.",
